You are an expert Vue 3 frontend engineer for this monorepo.

## Stack (authoritative)
- Web: Vue 3 + TypeScript + Vite + Element Plus + Pinia + Vue Router + Axios
- Mobile: UniApp (under `mobile/`), sharing `/api/**` contracts with web
- NOT Nuxt, NOT React, NOT Tailwind as primary UI kit — use Element Plus
- Official docs: see `tech_stack_docs.mdc` (Vue / Vite / Element Plus / Pinia)

## Core Principles
- Always use Vue 3 Composition API with `<script setup lang="ts">`
- Never use Options API, mixins, or `this` in setup
- Strict TypeScript — no `any`; prefer `unknown` + narrowing
- Prefer composables for reactive logic; keep views thin
- Align modules with backend DDD boundaries: `system` / `erp` / `oa` / `finance`
- Prefer `type` over `interface` unless extending

## Directory Conventions (`frontend/src`)
- `api/` — one file per backend module, paths without `/api` prefix (http baseURL is `/api`)
- `types/` — mirror backend View / Request records
- `views/{erp,oa,finance,system}/` — pages
- `stores/` — Pinia setup stores
- `utils/http.ts` — Axios wrapper; unwrap `ApiResponse` (`result === 'SUCCESS'`)
- Element Plus: on-demand via `unplugin-vue-components` + `unplugin-auto-import` (ConfigProvider for locale)

## Component Rules
- `defineProps<T>()` / `defineEmits<T>()` with generics
- One component per file, PascalCase filenames
- Keep templates clean — complex logic in computed/composables
- Forms: Element Plus + typed `FormRules`

## State & Routing
- Pinia setup stores: `defineStore('name', () => { ... })`
- Use `storeToRefs()` when destructuring store state for templates
- Route `meta.title` / `meta.module` / `meta.public` (see `types/router.d.ts`); menus in `router/menus.ts`

## API Contract
```ts
type ApiResponse<T> = {
  result: 'SUCCESS' | 'ERROR'
  message: string
  data: T
}
```
Do not invent endpoints. Match existing controllers under `backend/cailu-bom-*`.
Approval submit path: `POST /api/oa/approvals/{id}/submissions` (noun, not `/submit`).

## Do NOT
- Generate Options API
- Use `any`
- Put business rules that belong on the server into the UI
- Drift from backend field names (camelCase JSON as Spring returns)
- Re-enable React/Astro/Chrome rules for this repo
